  "title": "Erdős Problem #84",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "The cycle set of a graph $G$ on $n$ vertices is a set $A\\subseteq \\{3,\\ldots,n\\}$ such that there is a cycle in $G$ of length $\\ell$ if and only if $\\ell \\in A$. Let $f(n)$ count the number of possible such $A$.\nProve that $f(n)=o(2^n)$.\nProve that $f(n)/2^{n/2}\\to \\infty$.",
